<br/>
The protector also shows a single punch hole cutout for the front facing camera, positioned on the right side of the panel rather than in the center. Some earlier reports had suggested the cutout could end up centered, so the accessories offer a firmer answer on its placement. Since the &zwnj;iPhone Ultra&zwnj; is expected to use <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/touch-id/">Touch ID</a> rather than <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/07/three-new-apple-ultra-products-rumored/">Face ID</a>, it doesn't need the larger TrueDepth sensor array <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mask-face-id/">Face ID</a> requires, clearing the way for a single hole punch camera, which is a first for the iPhone. <br/>
<br/>
